// Found by a coverage-guided run of the FeasibleTargetsAreReachableWithSpilling property
// test: a pure 18-deep permutation. The shuffler converges to a state where only position 0
// -- beyond swap reach at target size -- is wrong: it demands v0, whose last on-stack copy
// sits correctly at position 9. Fixing position 0 requires moving that last copy into it
// while the stack is one short (the swap edge), but the swap rule refuses to move the last
// reachable copy of a value out of its position. Instead, the grow step dups v0 for the
// deficit, the fresh copy cannot travel below swap reach, and the shrink towards the
// unreachable position pops it again. The dup/pop pair cycles until MaxIterationsReached.
initial: [v2, v0, v0, v1, v2, v1, v3, v1, v3, v1, v2, v2, v3, v2, v1, v1, v3, v3]
targetStackTop: [v0, v1, v2, v1, v3, v1, v1, v2, v3, v0, v3, v2, v3, v2, v1, v1, v3, v2]
targetStackSize: 18
allowSpilling: true
